<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Printer on 0x32++</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/printer/</link><description>Recent content in Printer on 0x32++</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Wed, 10 Feb 2010 12:21:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/printer/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Poster Printer</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/poster-printer/</link><pubDate>Wed, 10 Feb 2010 12:21:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/poster-printer/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 14 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 19 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;div style="margin: 0px 2px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 1px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="padding: 4px; background-color: #c3d9ff;"&gt;&lt;h3 style="margin:0px 3px;font-family:sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 1px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 2px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="font-family:sans-serif;overflow:auto;width:100%;margin: 0px 10px"&gt;&lt;h2 style="margin: 0.25em 0 0 0"&gt;&lt;div class=""&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.ghacks.net/2010/02/10/poster-printer/"&gt;Poster Printer&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt; &lt;div style="margin-bottom: 0.5em"&gt;via &lt;a href="http://www.ghacks.net/" class="f"&gt;gHacks technology news&lt;/a&gt; by Martin on 2/10/10&lt;/div&gt; &lt;p&gt;Easy Poster Printer is a free software program for the Windows operating system that enables a user to create a poster out of an image or photo that is loaded into the software. Veteran users might already know the concept that is applied to those images from services such as &lt;a href="http://www.ghacks.net/2006/11/30/create-huge-rasterized-images-from-pictures/"&gt;Rasterbator&lt;/a&gt; or &lt;a href="http://www.ghacks.net/2008/10/30/create-large-wall-posters/"&gt;Block Posters&lt;/a&gt; which we reviewed earlier.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>